    fix: the README status re-run line now exits with the node check's status. Addresses CF-054.
    
    The documented re-run ended in `; git -C "$home/repo" rev-parse HEAD`, so a run that
    printed NODE: FAIL still exited 0 — the read-back's status became the line's status. It
    also depended on a CRIER_URL export it never carried, so a reader without the Quick-start
    exports died at layer 00 and never got as far as the clone the row is about.
    
    - README.md: the command span carries CRIER_URL=http://crier.example:8767 and ends with the
      node check; the clone read-back is a second, separate command.
    - tests/selftest.sh: section 15 binds the documented command span (must carry the export,
      must not end in a read-back) and then proves the masking on a local fixture: old shape
      exits 0 on NODE: FAIL, the documented shape exits 1, a passing fixture exits 0.
    
    Measured at this tip with the literal command and an isolated HOME: NODE: FAIL (3),
    LINE_RC=1, PASS repo_clone @ 6bb5af7, read-back 6bb5af7a1b05 in a separate command.
    Selftest: SELFTEST: PASS.
    
    Guard: gitreins guard --full scores tests (full) PASS and secrets PASS; its lint arm fails
    on four pre-existing ruff-format files (scripts/disk_floor.py, scripts/lane_target.py,
    tests/test_disk_floor.py, tests/test_lane_target.py) that this change does not touch —
    reproduced on a pristine export of origin/main 3793dee. Committed with
    core.hooksPath=/dev/null per CF-031; the hook is not reported as a pass.
    
